Geological Structures: a Practical Introduction — Waldron and Snyder (@geo-structures: 0, is #reference, #part-of @geo-sources) { r_2RC4KMK6ADFX90708NZH2F6RRW
John Waldron and Morgan Snyder. Geological Structures: a Practical Introduction. University of Alberta Library, 2020. DOI 10.29173/oer3. Ebook ISBN 978-1-55195-442-4. [Complete book and downloads](https://pressbooks.openeducationalberta.ca/introductorystructuralgeology/).

Read the entire book and complete its ten laboratory studies. It connects orientation, primary structures, cross-sections/three-point problems, stereographic projection, folds, fabrics, strain/stress, fractures, faults, field mapping, fold/thrust belts, shear zones, and impacts. Return to exact sections for an advanced interpretation rather than using only the diagrams.

The publisher states CC BY-NC 4.0 except where noted. Preserve authors, edition, DOI, publisher, and component notices. This is a substantial practical/academic spine; the unique mineralogy/petrology and geophysics subjects remain deeper studies. Metadata, contents, exercises, authorized formats, and licence checked on 29 October 2026. No book, exercise media, or field dataset is copied into the repository.

